{{--
    Write your message text BELOW this block. The block itself is a template
    comment: it is stripped at compile time and never becomes part of the message.

    Static text is sent verbatim, so you can write HTML formatting markup
    (<b>bold</b>, <i>italic</i>, <a href="https://example.com">link</a>) directly.

    Two interpolation forms:
      {{ $variable }}   — output an ESCAPED value (use for user data)
      {!! $variable !!} — output a RAW, unescaped value (use for trusted,
                          already-formatted content like translation strings)

    Values are passed in from the controller:
      view('welcome', ['name' => $user->first_name])
    The authenticated user is also available directly as $user.

    For multilingual bots, pull text from lang/{locale}/laragram.php with __().
    A translation carrying its own <b>bold</b> markup has to be output raw — but
    __() substitutes :placeholder values WITHOUT escaping them, so escape each
    substituted value yourself with e():
      {!! __('laragram.welcome.greeting', ['name' => e($name)]) !!}
    The locale is already set per user, so the right language is returned.
--}}
Hello! 👋 Edit <b>text.php</b> to write your message.
